From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-of-dwcmshc: power up SDIO-only slots in the rescan work

mmc_start_host() powers the card up during probe unless the host sets
MMC_CAP2_NO_PRESCAN_POWERUP. For the NanoKVM Wi-Fi slot that runs the
mmc-pwrseq-simple post-power-on delay (200 ms) inside the asynchronous
probe, and kernel_init() waits for all asynchronous probes before it
starts /init. An SDIO-only slot (no-sd and no-mmc) is now powered up by
the rescan work instead, which no initcall waits for.

Signed-off-by: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-dwcmshc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-dwcmshc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-dwcmshc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-of-dwcmshc.c
@@ -2450,6 +2450,15 @@
 	if (err)
 		goto err_bus_clk;
 
+	/*
+	 * An SDIO-only slot powers its card up in the rescan work, not here:
+	 * its power sequence may wait (200 ms for the NanoKVM Wi-Fi module),
+	 * and the kernel holds /init until every probe has returned.
+	 */
+	if ((host->mmc->caps2 & (MMC_CAP2_NO_SD | MMC_CAP2_NO_MMC)) ==
+	    (MMC_CAP2_NO_SD | MMC_CAP2_NO_MMC))
+		host->mmc->caps2 |= MMC_CAP2_NO_PRESCAN_POWERUP;
+
 	sdhci_get_of_property(pdev);
 
 	priv->vendor_specific_area1 =
